The three categories of inadequate disclosure that PS26/3 presumes create an unfair relationship under the motor finance redress scheme are:

1. Discretionary Commission Arrangements (DCAs);
2. High Commission payments, defined as 39% of the total cost of credit and 10% of the loan value;
3. Contractual ties that give a lender exclusivity or a right of first refusal. 

These categories are mentioned in the retrieved context where the FCA identifies features associated with unfair relationships under section 140A of the Consumer Credit Act 1974.

